OOPs: Object Oriented Programming Structure

-> our data will be safe
-> we can use the same method name and have different output
-> we can re-use the methods which are used in repeat mode
-> managing our code becomes a lot easier

 -Encapsulation: variables and methods needs to be placed within the class
   -Data Hiding
               : data[variables] should be hidden from other classes by making them private
               : we need to set the value of variables through the methods

 -Polymorphism
   -method overloading
   -method overriding

 Inheritance
   -abstraction
   -interface

A------------------------------------>B

i) He will not follow the traffic rules
   -> He might get into some accident because of his mistake
   -> He might be caught by traffic cop
   -> He might be fined by traffic cop
   -> He might be jailed for not following traffic rules
   -> He might get into into some road rage
   -> He might be both caught, fined & jailed
   -> He might reach his destination without any of the above action happening

ii) He will follow the traffic rules
    -> He will reach the destination